        "findings": [
          "Complete final Sets131/Proof219 source, both 10/10 and 7/8 focused audits, both original executed guards and both portable guards read CLEAN. Actual passed records and every selected recorded input/object were independently rehashed. No mathematical or checker defect found.",
          "The fixed Sigma1 sequent-image graph is total on all internal raw inputs via actual I-Sigma-1 HFS Sigma1 replacement. Its unique arithmetic image is chosen. This is neither object-level set-theoretic Choice nor a uniform proof-code selector. Formula typing and SHIFT equations keep their exact well-formedness premises.",
          "The proof induction fixes chosen and one internal total. Its changing level/offset are bounded universal quantifiers, with Delta1 source Derivation/budget tests and Sigma1 target Derivable. The arbitrary syntactic hAx resource is outside that induction predicate. No unbounded universal target proof premise or stronger induction is hidden.",
          "All ten actual Derivation.case constructors are handled: excluded middle, truth, conjunction, disjunction, ALL, EXISTS, weakening, SHIFT, cut and axiom. Actual source typing/equality premises are used. Strict child-code bounds pay for level+1 at ALL and offset+1 at zero-level SHIFT; positive-level SHIFT lowers level and applies the target SHIFT rule.",
          "At the root, total=d and level=offset=0 discharge the budget for every internal source proof code. Singleton sequent image gives actual Provable transport. ZF/ZFC endpoints discharge generic hAx using the checked literal axiom recognizers.",
          "Named GEN uses actual proof renaming plus the checked free_bindOneAt identity and the target ALL rule over the empty shifted context. Arbitrary internal chosen labels/formulas, including free zero, are covered. No closed-matrix or freshness premise remains.",
          "Final draft-to-pass proof delta is arithmetic side-placement normalization in two budget helpers, explicit depth0+1-to1 formula typing and two unused lambda names. No theorem statement or ten-rule case changed. Sets source/audit and Proof audit are unchanged from the historical source-first review.",
          "Sets kernel PASS is the first attempt,10probes/10callers. Proof run1 is a preserved elaboration FAIL and run2 is actual PASS7probes/8callers. Both final audits report only propext/Classical.choice/Quot.sound and zero warnings. Histories distinguish two unbuilt preparations, one FAIL and two PASS attempts; ten source/audit snapshots and original drivers are bound.",
          "Portable guards are frozen to exact source/audit/probe/caller identities. Current repo remapping occurs before import traversal, including Sets and all parent audits; cache overrides are hash-bound. Shared predecessor sources/objects must agree. Actual first external and required Lean/Omega providers match recorded source/object pairs and toolchain references, with before/after checks and compiler/dependency identities.",
          "All four override/relocated preflights remain PREPARED_NOT_BUILT with zero source/audit commands. Fourteen project objects relocate byte-for-byte while the Foundation namespace/external boundaries remain explicitly reused. Five recorded rejections cover optimized Python, nonempty output, wrong source, inconsistent shared parent object and fake actual Omega even with empty historical tool lists. These controls were read, not rerun.",
          "Guard metadata correctly states zero Lean proof builds; compiler lean --version queries occur during preparation/controls reaching compiler validation. No proof replay, compiler command or maintained/source edit was run by this reviewer."
        ],
        "nonclaims": [
          "No C254 twelve-rule proof-row/history decoding transport, accepted-code interpretation, PA consistency/nonhalting comparison or internal binary runtime theorem is established by this packet.",
          "Existential derivability preservation does not supply a deterministic represented proof-code transformation function.",
          "Selected source/object and immediate boundary checks do not attest every transitive object in the reused external namespace.",
          "At review time no 11 mapped maintained target files or maintained-default preflights were present; this packet binds publication sources, actual kernel records and four explicit override/relocation preparations. Later placement can be appended without proof replay."
